      "description": "A word search over names, titles and summaries. Call get_context before answering a question about company data. Find what is written down about a few words, by the names people use: metrics and their other names (such as GMV), markets, domains, member names from the data tool (such as payments.orders), and words in an item's title, summary or text. Use it for "what do we know about", "what is" or "how is it defined", and when you don't know the exact names. Filter by domain (a name such as Sales) or kind (event, warning, rule or guide). Returns the matching items, titles and summaries only, and for each metric or dimension the words name: the definition its source gives and what this context adds; and terms, each word a person defined in Definitions, with its meaning as written. When no words match, it returns the items that apply to what the words name, on the dates the window or the words give, or else today, as say says; when nothing is found, why says what to try. Read an item in full with read_context.",
